Starter PIDoc source for Astro Color Mixer v0.9.3-beta. Formal PixInsight documentation integration to be validated.

\title Astro Color Mixer
\section Overview

Script name: AstroColorMixer.js

Version: v0.9.3-beta

Astro Color Mixer is a PixInsight script for nonlinear RGB color and luminance refinement in astrophotography. It is intended for post-stretch finishing work on practical astro color bands, luminance-targeted masks, and sequential refinement passes.

\section Installation and Use

- Manual beta install currently uses Script > Execute Script.
- Repository-style installation will follow after update repository validation.
- Documentation resources are bundled under rsc/AstroColorMixer/docs/.

\section Basic Workflow

1. Open a nonlinear RGB image.
2. Choose Image Type: Stars Present or Starless.
3. Start with Base Pass.
4. Make broad H/S/L adjustments.
5. Use Width and Feather to refine color selection.
6. Use Range Mask for luminance-targeted work.
7. Add Refinement Passes for targeted cleanup.
8. Inspect preview, masks, histogram, polar plot, and probe.
9. Apply to New Image.
10. Save an Adjustment Set if needed.

\section Major Tool Areas

- Color Mixer
- Neutral / Low-Saturation
- Selected Band
- Range Mask
- Refinement Passes
- Preview and Mask Views
- Histogram / Polar Plot / Probe
- Adjustment Sets

\section Limitations

- not intended for linear calibration
- preview is downsampled
- extreme changes can artifact
- hue is unreliable in low-saturation regions
- Range Mask depends on stretch
- beta software status applies

\section Related Documents

See FAQ.pidoc for the practical guide and TechnicalAppendix.pidoc for the processing model summary.
